From ef9b6c059c8a579491c6ff7ecb6d627a6060caa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:53:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 145/168] mfd: mtk-spmi-pmic: Clear the RCS done flag after
 completing at probe

Writing RCS_IRQ_DONE at probe completes a request the bootloader left
pending, but with none pending the flag stays set. The Jolla Phone's
MT6363 then raises no further request: in boots where its key IRQs
never fired, 0x41b read 0x01 from probe on and no request ever reached
SPMI-M, although key presses latched in its PSC status; in the boot
where they worked it read 0x00. A done written for a real request is
cleared by the PMIC itself, so only probe needs this.

Clear the flag again after setting it.
---
 drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c b/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
index eab1e7a76..2aa700741 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
@@ -342,8 +342,13 @@ static int mtk_spmi_pmic_irq_init(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regmap,
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* Complete a request left pending at boot, or the PMIC sends no more */
+	/*
+	 * Complete a request left pending at boot, or the PMIC sends no more.
+	 * With none pending the done flag stays set and blocks the next one,
+	 * so clear it again.
+	 */
 	ret = regmap_write(regmap, MTK_SPMI_PMIC_RCS_IRQ_DONE, 1);
+	ret = ret ?: regmap_write(regmap, MTK_SPMI_PMIC_RCS_IRQ_DONE, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Cannot complete the RCS request\n");
 
